1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Midnight Marquee premieres in five minutes.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Six things can go wrong tonight: underpaid
royalties, a blank ad slot, a bot ring,

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,500
a region buffering out,
an audience quietly leaving.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:21,000
Most studios run six separate tools for these,
and none of them talk to each other.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Two specialists, two domains, two symptoms:
one root cause.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,500
Neither could have said it alone. The playback
agent cannot see ad revenue,

7
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:47,000
and the ads agent cannot see CDN telemetry.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:53,000
That correlation is the whole reason this is
a fleet, and not six demos.

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,500
In ADK this works only because specialists
are attached as tools that return findings.

10
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:03,000
As sub-agents they take the conversation
and never give it back.

11
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,500
Now the contract. Gemini reads the original
clause and turns prose into computable terms.

12
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:19,500
Units at the base rate, units at the escalated
rate, expected versus paid, and the gap.

13
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,000
Every number here is re-derived from the
warehouse. Nothing is a magic constant.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:31,000
That is forensic accounting a lawyer
can follow, not a dashboard.

15
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
One device fingerprint across ninety accounts,
corroborated by impossible travel.

16
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
The ring hides in a realistic crowd:
fan-out alone is not fraud.

17
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
And it consulted one specialist, not six.

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
A single-domain question. The orchestrator
routes; it does not fire at everything.

19
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
That report was not written for me.

20
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Cloud Scheduler called the fleet on the hour.
Control Room ran a standing brief,

21
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:14,500
two specialists queried ClickHouse, and filed
a root cause with a severity it chose itself,

22
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:17,500
with nobody watching.

23
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:22,000
A CDN node does not fail at a convenient hour.
The trigger is a clock, not a request.

24
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
The ground truth is in the repository.

25
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:38,500
This asserts every seeded anomaly against
the live database, and that the decoys exist,

26
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:41,500
so detection is not trivial.

27
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:47,000
ADK's rubric judge scores it on 23 rubrics.
Two check the agents do not invent findings.

28
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Six specialists, one ClickHouse foundation,
one orchestrator that connects the dots.

29
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:57,500
Gemini 2.5 on Vertex AI, the Agent
Development Kit, the ClickHouse MCP server.

30
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:00,000
Live. This is The Backlot.
